# RealtimeSanitizer suppressions for anira's CI (RTSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...).
#
# One known pre-existing violation class is suppressed so the job can gate
# everything else: anira's logging streams (LOG_ERROR/LOG_WARNING -> std::cerr/
# std::cout) flush from real-time paths in rare fallback branches, e.g. the
# "No free inference queue found" warning in Context::new_data_submitted and
# the RingBuffer overflow log. The fix (no logging from the audio thread) is
# tracked separately; suppressing by the ostream frames keeps the scope exactly
# "logging via streams" — allocations, locks, sleeps, and semaphore syscalls on
# real-time paths still abort the job.
call-stack-contains:basic_ostream
